ral related products under the Winger, Preview, Propose, and Nuvita brand names, as well as ProNutiva, a solution for crop protection. It also provides seeds for vegetables and crops, such as grain sorghum, forage, corn, canola, sunflower, rice, and wheat as well as other crops, including pearl millets, biofumingants, oats, mustards, and alfalfas under the Advanta, Alta Seeds, and Pacific Seeds brand names. In addition, the company offers industrial and specialty chemicals, such as phosphorus, cynation, phosgenation, and acrolein; other non-agricultural related products; post-harvest solutions; farmer education and engagement; environmental solutions; and apiculture services, as well as operates nurture.farm, a digital platform for growers, farming communities, and food systems. It serves input suppliers, distributors, farmers, food wholesalers/traders, food manufacturers, food retailers, consumers, industry associations, media, cooperatives, government, restaurants, agriculture chemical distributors, and non-government organisations. The company exports its products. The company was formerly known as United Phosphorus Limited and changed its name to UPL Limited in October 2013. UPL Limited was founded in 1969 and is based in Mumbai, India.","beta":0.523,"sharesOutstanding":844169318,"marketCap":477585539072,"trailingPE":25.257,"forwardPE":12.4141,"priceToBook":1.3688,"enterpriseToEbitda":10.388,"dividendYield":1.08,"heldPercentInsiders":0.3373,"heldPercentInstitutions":0.45,"earningsGrowth":-0.26,"revenueGrowth":-0.013,"website":"https://www.upl-ltd.com","fullTimeEmployees":12399,"recommendationKey":"buy","targetMeanPrice":654.353,"numberOfAnalystOpinions":17,"financialCurrency":"INR"},"estimates":{"eps":{"0q":{"avg":15.0,"low":15.0,"high":15.0,"yearAgoEps":4.69,"numberOfAnalysts":1.0,"growth":2.1983,"currency":"INR","methodology":"normalized"},"+1q":{"avg":27.09,"low":27.09,"high":27.09,"yearAgoEps":null,"numberOfAnalysts":1.0,"growth":null,"currency":"INR","metho